# /etc/default/limine — written by install.sh (target-setup.sh) from
# install/files/default-limine.in. Read by limine-mkinitcpio-hook
# (limine-update) and limine-snapper-sync; overrides their own configs.
# Machine-specific (LUKS UUID, resume offset) — change it with care and
# run "sudo limine-update" afterwards.

ESP_PATH="/boot"

# Root, LUKS and hibernation: generated at install time.
KERNEL_CMDLINE[default]+=" @@CMDLINE@@"
# Quiet boot for Plymouth (from Omarchy, MIT): initramfs_async=0 avoids a
# race that drops Plymouth to a plain text LUKS prompt on newer kernels;
# console=dumb avoids a rare hang at "Starting Switch Root".
KERNEL_CMDLINE[default]+=" quiet splash loglevel=3 rd.udev.log_level=3 systemd.show_status=false vt.global_cursor_default=0 initramfs_async=0 systemd.tty.term.console=dumb"

# UKI: kernel + initramfs + cmdline in one .efi (decisions: Secure Boot in v3).
ENABLE_UKI=yes
CUSTOM_UKI_NAME="golden"

# Menu: CachyOS kernel first, then linux-lts, then snapshots.
TARGET_OS_NAME="Golden"
BOOT_ORDER="linux-cachyos, *, *fallback, Snapshots"
FIND_BOOTLOADERS=yes

# limine-snapper-sync: last 10 snapshots in the menu (decisions §4).
# Our snapshots live in the top-level subvolume @.snapshots, not in the
# default nested /@/.snapshots.
MAX_SNAPSHOT_ENTRIES=10
ROOT_SUBVOLUME_PATH="/@"
ROOT_SNAPSHOTS_PATH="/@.snapshots"
